<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The Developer ID build (7j, B1′; user 2026-09-12): no App Sandbox. Inside it, accessibility calls to other apps
	     fail even with the accessibility server's lookup allowed — a scratch copy without it read Finder's and
	     TextEdit's windows at once. What stays is Formora's own fence: file tools inside the project folder, commands
	     and computer use behind approval. Debug builds are this build; the App Store build keeps the sandbox. -->
	<!-- Under the hardened runtime, Apple events are refused without asking unless this is present (old phase 0). -->
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- 2026-09-15: the shipped dmg is ad-hoc signed (no Team ID). Under the hardened runtime, library validation
	     then refuses every embedded framework ("mapping process and mapped file have different Team IDs"), so 1.0.3
	     and 1.0.4 quit on launch before running any of our code — the first builds to embed Sparkle.framework.
	     Xcode builds never showed it: they carry the developer's Team ID on both sides. Notarization allows this
	     exception, so it stays when the app is Developer ID signed. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
